// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/fpga/wasm_board_ax7203.t27 -- a WASM-executing cell on the ALINX AX7203, one spec
; Board phase (P1) of the epic gHashTag/trinity-fpga#917: AI-generated FPGA hardware that
; executes WASM. Everything between the UART pins is this file; the RTL is generated by t27c
; and never hand-written. The only foreign Verilog in the build is the board top that supplies
; the STARTUPE2 config-oscillator clock and the pins, flagged for the owner label
; owner-approved-foreign on the pull request; the XDC is the existing gf16_clean_ax7203.xdc,
; reused byte for byte.
; -
; WHY. The MVP spec specs/fpga/wasm_interp.t27 proved the interpreter as executable t27: 23
; opcodes, 16 real WASM bodies, 25 checks, icarus green, but no ports and no clock. This cell
; puts that engine on silicon: the same one-opcode-per-clock execution, reached through a real
; UART, on a real board, checked against a golden fixed before the run.
; -
; THE MACHINE. One clock does one thing: a piece of one UART frame, or one WASM opcode. The
; tick body step_all is a plain fn (a task in the generated Verilog, drivable from the tests)
; and on_clock wraps it for the ports. The task keeps blocking assigns, so the tests in this
; file and the silicon clock run the identical sequential body; the sections are ordered so
; every strobe (rxnew, frame_go) is consumed one tick after it is produced. The engine is the
; Verilog-lowerable subset: u32 scalars, u8 bytes, indexed array reads and writes, flat
; if/else opcode dispatch, no loops in the tick body. Programs are the MVP bodies byte for byte
; plus structured control flow (issue #12010): block, loop, br, br_if and br_table over a
; label stack of LABEL_MAX frames, one LEB byte per label. A branch forward skips its bytes
; one per engine step through a syntactic scan that steps over immediates, so an 0x0B inside
; an immediate is never read as an end; FUEL_MAX fetches end a run with ERR_FUEL, so no
; program can hang the link. Still missing: if/else, call, globals, i64 and the float
; families, and every linear memory beyond the one 64 KiB page of P5 below; a function-level
; br answers ERR_LABEL (return exists), a label of more than one LEB byte answers ERR_LEB.
; THE ALU HAS ONE HOME. The 24 single-clock i32 ALU opcodes (the ten compares, add, sub, the
; eight bitwise/shift/rotate bytes, eqz, clz, ctz, popcnt) are not 24 hand-copied branches:
; alu_arity(op) says how many operands a byte pops (0 = not an ALU byte) and alu_eval(op, a,
; b) is the value it pushes, each written once below. The tick takes one arm for all 24, and
; specs/fpga/wasm_opcodes.t27 `use`s this module and calls the same two functions as its
; oracle, so the table's expected values and the silicon's cannot be two different algorithms
; (issue #12011). The direction is forced: t27c gen-verilog imports only enums and structs
; from a used module, never a function body, so the bodies live in the module that is lowered.
; P2 widens the set: multi-byte signed LEB for i32.const (an operand-fetch submachine in the
; shape of the mul microsequence), drop, select, the unsigned compares, clz/ctz/popcnt,
; shr_u, rotl/rotr, and div/rem signed and unsigned (a 32-clock restoring divider), plus the
; program store loaded over the wire. The MVP spec keeps proving what this cell does not run.
; P5 (issue #12202) adds linear memory, ONE 64 KiB page and nothing larger: i32.load,
; load8_s/u, load16_s/u, i32.store, store8, store16, memory.size and memory.grow. The page is
; `var mem : [MEM_BYTES]u8`, shaped for block RAM: one read OR one write per engine step, the
; address registered (mem_addr) a step before its data is used, and a 2- or 4-byte access is a
; byte-per-step microsequence in the mul/divide shape, little-endian. MEASURED, NOT BLOCK RAM
; YET: yosys 0.67 read_verilog on the generated file answers "Replacing memory \mem with list
; of registers" (the page is written inside the `always @(posedge clk or negedge rst_n)` that
; gen-verilog emits for on_clock; a one-line on_clock probe with a nonblocking write gave the
; same warning; the cause inside yosys is not isolated; compiler gap recorded in the pull
; request). Until that lowering changes the page is 65536 x 8 register bits in synthesis, and
; no claim of block RAM is made here. The memarg (align, then
; offset, two LEB128 u32) has its own submachine: align is read and ignored, a fifth byte of
; either that continues answers ERR_LEB, and so does an offset whose fifth byte carries bits
; above 2^32 (it would wrap). The effective address is base + offset as a 33-bit sum; an
; access of w bytes whose sum exceeds MEM_BYTES - w answers ERR_MEM before any byte is written,
; so there is no wrap and a trapping store leaves the page as it was. memory.size pushes 1;
; memory.grow pops its delta and pushes 0xFFFFFFFF for every delta, 0 included (a documented
; deviation: WASM answers the old size for 0); both carry the reserved memory-index byte,
; which must be 0. Fuel stays one unit per fetch: the extra clocks of a multi-byte access add
; none. The page is declared zero-filled (a repeat, not a 65536-element literal); gen-verilog
; emits no initial block for it, so an iverilog run reads X from a byte nobody wrote and no
; test here reads a byte before it stores it (compiler gap recorded in the pull request).
; -
; THE WIRE. The TRI-NET node link, the one that carried 1035886/1035886 TNF16 requests and
; 251616/251616 mxdot4 requests at 1144744 baud with none lost: CFGMCLK between 65.6 and
; 68.7 MHz, divider 60, one start bit, 8 data bits LSB first, one stop bit.
;   Request  SYNC0 SYNC1 OP SEQ SA SB A0..A15 B0..B15            38 bytes
;   OP is a program id, SEQ is echoed, SA SB and A4..A15 B4..B15 are zero, and the operands
;   are x = A0..A3 little-endian and y = B0..B3 little-endian, both raw u32 with no range
;   limit: the LEB range limits only constants inside program bodies.
;   Response RESP_OK SEQ y0 y1 y2                                5 bytes
;   The word on the wire is the low 24 bits of the u32 result, little-endian. The engine is
;   full 32-bit inside; 24 bits is the response width of this link. Board vectors come in two
;   kinds: exact vectors, whose full result already fits the word, and low-24 vectors (the
;   wraparound and the negative-constant programs), where the golden is the low 24 bits of the
;   full u32 and full-width exactness stays pinned by the MVP spec in simulation.
;   An unknown OP or any engine error (bad opcode, stack underflow or overflow, local index,
;   LEB continuation, program counter past end, label out of range, fuel spent, memory access
;   outside the page) answers RESP_BADOP SEQ 0 0 0.
; -
; WHAT A PASS SAYS. This RTL receives real WASM program ids and operands over a UART, executes
; one WASM opcode per clock, and answers with the exact result, on this board, for every
; vector listed here, against a golden built by the host runner from the same program bytes.
; WHAT IT DOES NOT SAY. Nothing about speed beyond one opcode per clock (a taken branch is
; two engine steps plus one per skipped byte), nothing about programs outside the opcode set
; named above, and nothing about formats: the response word is 24 bits by the wire, not by
; the engine.
; ASCII only, English only.

module fpga_wasm_board;

pub const KIND : str = "board-cell";
pub const ID : str = "fpga/wasm_board_ax7203";
